+The Home padlock marks Basic Privacy, Enhanced Privacy or AES-256 with a usable transmit key. The transmit screen
+shows it during encrypted voice PTT. On receive it marks a caller whose protected burst was passed to the voice decoder
+through the configured privacy path. This is a playback indicator and does not authenticate the key. When the cipher
+withholds protected voice, the call says "Encrypted: not played".
 
 The key is set over the debug link (RADIO op 19, `radio_req_dmr_privacy`). The radio core saves it in settings slot 1
